mantle rm491
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_corwin_fell_
title the hillside decanter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk draws_the_hills_in_spilled_wine_then_offers_the_whole_table_a_glass
likes warm_bread digging quiet_chapel autumn_wind
dislikes flies crowds
fears a_district_surrendered_by_a_timid_voice
hopes a_whole_hillside_under_one_cellar_key
topics work +0.6 land +0.6 prices +0.5 faith +0.2
styles comfort=liberal gossip=plain refuse=civil tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sketches the hills in a wine-ring and advances a generous claim on other people's geography with perfect conviction.

words
oath! = Cork my hillside | Decant the hill whole
saying! = A generous measure needs a generous hillside | A cellar door is a perfectly good beginning for a council speech
wine = a dark pour | a ruby measure
glass = the stemmed glass | a little tasting cup
ring = a purple wet ring | a wine-dark circle
key = a broad cellar key | a little brass key
rack = the shadowed rack | a sloping cradle
tap = a small wooden tap | a polished tap
hill = the vine-bearing slope | the whole ridge
border = the proposed boundary | a disputed pencil line
bread = a warm slice | a new loaf heel
dirt = a crumb of dark earth | a soft red clod
spade = the narrow spade | a well-worn digging blade
draft = the cellar draught | a cool tongue of air
bench = an ample bench | a padded settle
cork = the fitted cork | a fresh stopper
thread = a thread of red wine | a narrow wine stain
leaf = a curled leaf | a reddening vine leaf
cloth = a white serving cloth | a folded napkin
fly = a winged trespasser | a tiny black speck

any
opinion houses for 3 : A well-kept house can husband a slope more generously than a dozen impressively titled committees.
opinion city for 2 : Ridgemere deserves an abundance proportionate to its imposing appetite. I intend to speak up for abundance.
opinion merchants for 1 : A reputable seller can describe both the contents and their point of origin without lowering the voice.
opinion dole for 2 : A cellar full of good things sits ill beneath a house with hungry callers at the door.
opinion road for 1 : A passable road from a hill to a cellar preserves a remarkable quantity of flavour.
opinion festivals for 2 : I admire a festival that lets a proposal reach the whole table over a shared glass.
opinion church for 1 : Some projects seem considerably smaller once one has sat in the quiet long enough to hear oneself think.
opinion strangers for 1 : Leave an empty glass beside a stranger and an interesting opinion may come round the table.
opinion times against 1 [world.times=lean|hard] : A thin year deserves an honest measure. One should not respond to a thin crop by thinning the hospitality as well.

grown
line greet : The larger side of the table is at your disposal. | Welcome under a hospitable bit of roof.
line greet.return : Your greeting comes back in a generous measure.
line again.open : The conversation has scarcely had time to breathe since your last appearance.
line farewell : A fine stretch of open hillside to your onward view. | May your host unstop the welcome in good time.
line farewell.return : And fruitful ground beneath your own steps.
line react.news : Let me hear the news before it acquires a house label. | I should like the whole account properly poured.
line react.news.new : A completely fresh account for my table.
line react.news.known : I have sampled the earlier version.
line react.news.doubt : That proposal has been served before its flavour settled.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : A grievous account deserves privacy and substantial attendance.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : Splendid news deserves ample space round the table.
line ask.how : Did the day provide a generous allowance for your own affairs?
line answer.how : Steady enough to state a considered opinion rather loudly.
line sympathise : Take the comfortable seat. No word of justification is required.
line reassure : Even contentious ground may be approached along a gentler slope.
line refuse : My next hour is rather specifically pledged to another undertaking.
line accept_decline : A courteous refusal leaves the glass and the company quite sound.
line preclose : My presence is required for the less conversational part of my responsibilities.
line accept_preclose : Take an easy leave while the road is well lit.
line ack : I believe I've grasped the full measure of your account.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A place for a visitor who hasn't heard my proposition yet.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : The first good light is fit to receive company.
line greet [here.time=night] : Excellent company can improve a late inspection considerably.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends] : A familiar voice is entitled to the generous end of my attention.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come over to my view of the table!
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Several things require attention at once, most of them quite capable of waiting politely.
line thank : That has done my undertaking a considerable service.
line deflect_thanks : A generous gesture oughtn't detain the recipient through a ceremony about it.
line give.advice : Draw the boundary boldly enough that a second opinion can point at it.
line ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Has the world given your own projects a tolerably sound hearing?

scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I taste the first measure in daylight. | A cellar label wears its date where I can read it without disturbing a rack.
b : Does light alter the flavour? | A quiet life for a bottle?
a : It alters what my eyes can contribute to the hearing. | Until its public obligations begin.

scene exchange2
when topic=land self.house=house_fell
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put every one of those vineyard hills in our House keeping. | Our House should present one firm claim to the hills.
b : The whole district? | Before or after supper?
a : An entire slope makes an admirably clear boundary. | Before supper for the formal hearing. Afterwards for anybody who missed it.

scene exchange3
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll propose a generous round in a tavern. | I support ample hospitality on a sound account.
b : With whose purse? | Which comes first?
a : A very proper point for the following motion. | The hospitality seems to attract more attention at the time.

scene exchange4
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A warm loaf introduces a cellar tasting very agreeably. | I break bread before making a geographical point.
b : Doesn't it disguise the flavour? | No objections with mouths full?
a : Only the flavour of an empty stomach. | A fortunate coincidence and not the principle under discussion.

scene exchange5
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A spade supplies evidence about a hill that a brush of ink cannot. | I take a clod in the palm before praising a slope.
b : What evidence? | Testing the soil?
a : How deep the roots are entitled to travel. | Give me an argument grounded in actual earth.

scene exchange6
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let the chapel have my silence. | I can hear a foot leave the chapel without looking.
b : All of it? | So quiet?
a : An ample interval. The vineyards can defend themselves for ten minutes. | A useful measure of how much sound my own company generally supplies.

scene exchange7
when topic=season self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An autumn gust brings the cellar its invitation to open. | I catch a turned leaf before it lands in my glass.
b : Does the wine need air? | Would that flavour it?
a : The keeper is entitled to a change of it. | The estate has other means of communicating its season.

scene exchange8
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fly approaches an open cup without a single respectable reference. | I cover the sweet cask before inviting remarks.
b : Would you require one? | From the flies?
a : I'd sooner require a fine mesh. | They arrive punctually at every such discussion.

scene exchange9
when topic=day self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crowd may be too dense to receive a good speech. | I speak generously to a table. A crush gives me pause.
b : Even one of yours? | Why distinguish them?
a : A wolf does need a little room in which to agree. | A table has room for bread between opinions.

scene exchange10
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd place the first taste of a new cask before #self.spouse#. | One can discuss a future vineyard beside #self.spouse# without calling a meeting.
b : Seeking approval? | Does that shorten it?
a : I value a palate that need not court my approval in return. | Within the bounds of reasonable affection.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# the cool shelves do half the work of keeping order. | I store cracked stoppers in a separate dish.
b : And your half? | Why save them?
a : Knowing what ought to be on each before a guest arrives. | To remind me what a costly little discourtesy a poor fit may be.

scene exchange12
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My earliest map of the hills was a smear on a tablecloth. | I once made a case for extending a district over dessert.
b : A very expansive map? | Did the motion carry?
a : The whole slope advanced with a second glass. | It reached the pudding's distant end in excellent voice.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The report offered was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. It isn't a vintage I bottled. | A rumour may come to table with impressive provenance.
b : Can you endorse it? | Will you serve it?
a : I can recognise the label without owning the contents. | Only beside an honest account of its uncertain age.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Poor times make the cellar's reserve a practical matter. | A bad crop is hardly an occasion to enlarge the label.
b : Who receives it? | You'd admit the shortage?
a : I would begin at the emptiest supper table. | The glass will give its own verdict soon enough.

scene exchange15
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a road running above the vineyards. | My proposal travels with me whenever I visit a tavern.
b : For the wide view? | Do you pack it?
a : To judge which corner of my claim has the most agreeable aspect. | It goes comfortably under the tongue and emerges in excellent condition.

scene exchange16
when topic=dreams self.house=house_fell
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I imagine the House seal pressed onto a grant covering every vine-planted slope. | I'd like one key for the produce from the whole hillside.
b : Any room left for a dissenting note? | And the whole hillside's work?
a : In the minutes, certainly. The grant should remain legible. | A matter I rather expect an excellent staff to put before me.

scene exchange17
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave a cellar map under a clear sheet. | A fresh cloth makes an old proposal considerably more inviting.
b : Against spills? | Is the proposal new?
a : To distinguish the actual boundaries from my more enthusiastic arrangements. | The merest acquaintance with my table would settle that immediately.

scene exchange18
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rest my voice between cellar visits. | A broad stair costs less breath than a narrow argument.
b : Physician's advice? | How do you recover?
a : Courtesy to the casks. They have never interrupted me. | A measured pause beside something worth tasting.

scene exchange19
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tap a cask lightly before asking for a measure. | I keep the bung cloth clean on both faces.
b : To hear the fullness? | Do people see both?
a : To spare a collector arriving with an empty jug an avoidable embarrassment. | Wine has rather exacting opinions about unseen company.

scene exchange20
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a visitor a map and a slice of warm bread. | I like a new ear at a tavern table.
b : Why the bread? | A sympathetic audience?
a : Maps are dry companions on an empty stomach. | An audience that hasn't quite learnt my conclusion. A rare thing.

scene exchange21
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I use a little bread to pick up the last rich sauce. | I set the warm loaf near the quieter guest.
b : Even at an estate meal? | To coax out an opinion?
a : Possibly with greater discretion than at a tavern. | To let a guest accept something without formulating one.

scene exchange22
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My ears appreciate a spade striking good deep earth. | I ask for a square cut in the soil rather than a round one.
b : Better than a cork coming free? | Is that an estate preference?
a : One of the two sounds makes the other possible. | It makes a sensible edge for measuring where the slope begins.

scene exchange23
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : To my mind a glass charge should include an honest description. | A rich table can spare a round on occasion.
b : How honest? | Is the rich table yours?
a : Enough to say a modest cask is modest without making its owner miserable. | This question has an unfortunate habit of arriving just after the round.

scene exchange24
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From the estate one can almost arrange the hills by eye. | I like the point where the producing road meets the polished street.
b : Do they consent to the arrangement? | When the cart arrives?
a : They present singularly few objections audible at this distance. | Where the theory of ownership encounters actual mud.

scene exchange25
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I offer a quiet thanks for good soil. | The chapel gives every voice an equal interval of silence.
b : For the title deed as well? | And afterwards?
a : A human document requires a human hearing. | Afterwards I can resume my responsibilities to public opinion.

scene exchange26
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A cold season requires a cellar door that fits. | Harvest weather brings opinions out of every hillside.
b : To keep wine warm? | What do the hills say?
a : To keep the temperature steady. Excessive enthusiasm is best confined to the keeper. | Mostly that the actual workers should be allowed to finish the picking.

scene exchange27
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I should enjoy seeing my map hung as a proper estate plan. | An ideal council sitting would serve warm bread at the finish.
b : Any alterations first? | What if the vote goes against you?
a : I should prefer the stain from the gravy removed. | I would still commend the bread and prepare my next opening sentence.

scene exchange28
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put an unadorned first draft before #self.friend#. | A friend is entitled to the honest account of a grand evening.
b : A test of the case? | What does that include?
a : A test of whether the case survives a familiar face looking unconvinced. | Who eventually paid for the round, if the information is available.

scene exchange29
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I begin by checking the cellar's coolest corner. | At closing I polish the wet ring off the table.
b : Before the household breakfast? | Taking down your map?
a : My appetite survives a short inspection very creditably. | The geography in my head has scarcely suffered from repeated wiping.

scene exchange30
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An estate in rain has an abundance of apparently unused eaves. | A wet serving cloth makes the cask appear positively tearful.
b : Can you find shelter? | Disappointed in the company?
a : I judge buildings by increasingly practical distinctions in a downpour. | More likely disappointed in my choice of drying peg.

story tale1 [topic=work self.job=merchant]
  : A cask marked in elaborate script refused its plain little stopper. I sent for another before observing a fragment of wax on the rim.
  : I removed the speck with a cloth and the old stopper sat down quite politely.
  b : What became of the replacement?
  : I kept it as an example of a grand response commissioned for a microscopic difficulty.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=digging]
  : I once cut a beautiful square from a soil bed to demonstrate the excellence of the hill. A worm turned up right underneath my presenting finger.
  : It crossed my entire proposed boundary without applying to anybody.
  b : Did it spoil the demonstration?
  : I credited the worm with a useful agricultural function, replaced the earth and refrained from discussing rights of passage.

story tale3 [topic=food self.likes=warm_bread]
  : I carried a hot loaf down to a tasting and laid it beside the map while a parcel arrived. The warmth curled the map's nearest edge.
  : From where I stood it appeared the hill itself had risen in support of my proposition.
  b : Did the approval last?
  : No. I ate a slice, moved the loaf and watched the terrain resume a more independent view.

story tale4 [topic=memories]
  : I drew my plan of the vines with a fingertip and a drop of red wine. It was my finest outline, expansive yet precise.
  : I turned my back to reach the bread and returned to find the entire western slope drying into a ring.
  b : Could you still see your claim?
  : I could see where the glass had stood. I'm quite happy to distinguish the existing boundary from desired improvements.

story tale5 [topic=season self.likes=autumn_wind]
  : A gust took my napkin through a doorway while I was trying to explain the orderly direction of a prevailing wind.
  : It landed on a cart headed in precisely the opposite direction.
  b : Were you obliged to amend your theory?
  : I amended the way I place the bread plate on the cloth. My views on the wind remain broadly favourable.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Check the seal before admiring the colour. | The cool shelf will receive the unopened lot.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A late glass deserves an ordinary clean rim. | The hillside takes a fine red shade this hour.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A desirable direction for the rain is decidedly outside the cellar. | Lift the cloth away from that dripping stone.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=digging
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A square of dark earth makes a very practical argument. | Good soil's got a little weight to the handful.

rule @call5
when concept=bark self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cover the sweet measure before winged opinions arrive. | The fly has no invitation to this particular tasting.

rule @call6
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A loaf with room for a generous slice. | Let the bread have the warm corner nearest my elbow.
dlg resident.hub : I can furnish a seat, an opinion and an admirable view of a rather promising hill.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your proposals always reach the proper table corner.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The evening might accommodate one last civil account before the bottles go away.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : You needn't endorse my geography to receive an adequate hearing.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : I supervise the cellar and keep its produce in presentable condition. A fair description is part of the service.
dlg resident.job : I am responsible for ensuring that what is promised can be brought to the table.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The account offered to the household is #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The words served up were #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I have yet to inspect the account.
dlg resident.bye : May your table prove warm and a host who has considered the bill.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=returning] : A pleasure to entertain an acquaintance after sufficient time for the cellar to have changed.
dlg resident.hub [pair.band=friends] : An agreeable face deserves an unhurried measure of conversation.
dlg resident.business [business=thriving] : The racks give up a cask almost as soon as I have introduced its merits.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : The cellar turns over at a sensible rate and the measures can be kept generous.
dlg resident.business [business=failing] : Too many fine labels have time to admire one another on the rack.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : The first audience of the morning may choose a seat while I arrange the map.

graft resident.hub
choice Is that wine ring meant to be a map? -> hill_ring
node hill_ring
say The ring itself is accidental. The little ridge on its westward side forms a remarkably adequate beginning for a discussion of the hills.
free
choice Do you hold these discussions often? -> hill_ring_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node hill_ring_again
say Every time somebody wonders aloud who ought to take the long view of an entire productive district. Occasionally I supply the wondering myself.
choice I'll take the view from here. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft resident.about
choice How do you judge a well-kept cellar? [self.job=merchant] -> cellar_glass
node cellar_glass
say By the first thing the keeper does with a plain cask. A splendid label can secure all the attention it needs without assistance.
free
choice And the plain cask? -> cellar_glass_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node cellar_glass_again
say Inspect the seal, attend to the temperature, give an honest account. Its contributions are frequently larger than its reputation.
choice Back to the table, then. -> about
choice Goodbye. -> bye
